       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg per dose four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. That is five times the maximum recommended ibuprofen dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day as an inpatient and 1,200 mg/day over the counter. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day and a common regimen.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg per dose is deliberate, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still want to add a note to the order about the dose."
