       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen is well into the toxic range. It isn't a dose that can be justified for any indication, and it could seriously harm the patient. Their normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day). The inpatient maximum is 3,200 mg/day, for example 800 mg four times daily.\n- **Help with pain control that needs more than ibuprofen.** I can enter ibuprofen at a safe dose alongside scheduled acetaminophen or another agent.\n- **Check a different intended dose.** If \"4000\" was meant to be something else, such as 400 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you think there's a real clinical need for this dose, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy or toxicology and placing the order directly through your institution's override process. I can't enter it myself."
      }
